{"name":"Alpine Goat","hex":"#f1f2f8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alpine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or inhabiting mountains, especially above the timberline.","Alternative letter-case form of Alpine: Of, relating to, or inhabiting the Alps, a large mountain range in Europe."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants, native to mountain habitats, often grown in rock gardens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alpine"},{"term":"goat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any ruminant of the genus Capra.\n\n The meat of these animals.","The meat of these animals."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To allow goats to feed on.","To scapegoat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alpine (American goat breed)","blocks":[{"text":"The Alpine is a North American breed of medium- to large-sized domestic goat of dairy type. It may be horned or polled and has a straight facial profile and erect ears; various coloration patterns are accepted, others are disallowed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Annie_BC.jpg/330px-Annie_BC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpine_(American_goat_breed)"},{"title":"British Alpine","blocks":[{"text":"The British Alpine is a British breed of dairy goat bred in the early twentieth century. It is black with white Swiss markings on the face."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Goat_at_Offley_-_geograph.org.uk_-_245154_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Goat_at_Offley_-_geograph.org.uk_-_245154_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Alpine"},{"title":"Goat","blocks":[{"text":"The goat or domestic goat is a species of goat-antelope that is mostly kept as livestock. It was domesticated